    {
      "action": "insert",
      "table": "academic_rule_sets",
      "key": {
        "program_id": "7100DIPLT",
        "rule_scope": "ADMISSION",
        "rule_name": "OFFICIAL_ADMISSION_REQUIREMENTS"
      },
      "before": null,
      "after": {
        "exact_choice_count": null,
        "notes": "Scheduled intakes September of even-numbered years. The next intake of this program is September 2026. Application processing Applications accepted October 1st* to March 1st.* We recommend that you apply early . All supporting documents must be submitted by the application deadline. Applicant residence requirement : This program is currently restricted to residents of Western Canada, including the provinces of British Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan, and Manitoba. Residents of other areas of Canada and international students are not being considered at this time. View programs that accept international students . *or next business day Entrance requirements Admission to this program is highly competitive. In 2022, BCIT admitted 1 in 3 applicants. Successful applicants exceeded entrance requirements. They had a clear understanding of the profession, manual dexterity, and interpersonal skills. Competitive Entry: Three-step process Preference will be given to applicants with: Related experience and exposure at Prosthetics and Orthotics clinics The following preferred post-secondary academic level courses: 6.0 credits of Human Anatomy and Physiology 3.0 credits of Physics (biomechanics is NOT accepted) 3.0 credits of Statistics 3.0 credits of Psychology (sport psychology is NOT accepted) Additional related post-secondary academic courses Requirements, experience, and above courses completed within the last five years Applicants with preferred entrance requirements are to submit transcripts and supporting documentation with their online application. Step 1: Meet the following entrance requirements English language proficiency: Category 2 \u2013 English Studies 12 (67%) or equivalent A recognized bachelor's degree in any field (120 credits) Complete the following form for submission with your online application: Mandatory Applicant Questionnaire [PDF] Read more about how to meet BCIT\u2019s entrance requirements Applicants currently enrolled in the last term of their degree/diploma must be on track to complete by May. If this applies to you, submit both of the following documents from your post-secondary institution: Transcript of completed courses Confirmation of enrolment letter verifying your current course enrolment and registration in the final term of your degree/diploma Applicants who have completed post-secondary studies outside of Canada, the United States, the United Kingdom, Australia or New Zealand will require a comprehensive evaluation of their credentials by the International Credential Evaluation Service (ICES) . Credential evaluation reports from other Canadian services may be considered. These reports must include course-by-course evaluations and GPA calculations. If you are not certain whether a course you have taken will qualify as one of the preferred courses listed above, please email a detailed course outline (more detailed than a course description) to lschubert4@bcit.ca . Step 2: Multiple Mini Interviews (MMIs) for shortlisted applicants All qualified applications will be reviewed by the program selection committee after the application deadline. Applications are assessed and scored based on each applicant\u2019s academic strength, completion of the preferred courses, related experience, and responses on the Mandatory Applicant Questionnaire. Shortlisted applicants will be contacted to attend an online Multiple Mini Interview (MMI). More details, specific instructions, and scheduling options will be provided to qualifying applicants. Step 3: Conditionally selected applicants Based on applications and performance on the MMIs, successful candidates will be selected and contacted with a conditional acceptance offer. If you have been conditionally accepted to BCIT you will be notified and will be required to pay a commitment fee and provide the following information to be accepted into the program: Criminal Record Check [PDF] Immunization Review [PDF] Submit to Student Health Services . Immunization is a mandatory requirement for this program. For instructions and more information, visit Student Health Services\u2019 Health Science Student Information . Once these and any other outstanding conditions have been met, you will receive notification of your full acceptance. Application timeline : October 1 : Applications open March 1 : Applications close Late March : Short-listed applicants are contacted to schedule MMIs Early April : MMIs are conducted Late April/Early May : Conditional offers of admissions are sent to selected applicants International applicants This program is not available to international students. View available programs . Applicant residence requirement : This program is currently restricted to residents of Western Canada, including the provinces of British Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan, and Manitoba. Residents of other areas of Canada and international students are not being considered at this time. Apply to program Note: The September 2026 intake is now closed for new applications. Applications for the September 2028 intake will be accepted starting October 1, 2027. To submit your application: Include proof of meeting all entrance requirements. Convert all transcripts and supporting documents to PDF files . Have a credit card ready to pay the application fee. Apply Now Learn more about how to apply myCommunication Within two business days of submitting your completed application, BCIT will send a message to your personal and myBCIT email addresses. All correspondence regarding your application will be posted to your online myCommunication account at my.bcit.ca . We will send you an email when a new message is posted. It is important to watch for these emails or regularly check your account online. You can expect to receive communication concerning the status of your application within four weeks. Go back Overview Next up Costs & Supplies",
